8--> EKSCTL Tool
     --> Check https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/eksctl/what-is-eksctl.html
	 
	 -->eksctl is a command-line tool used to create and manage Kubernetes clusters on AWS EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service). 
	    It automates many AWS configuration steps that you would otherwise perform manually. 
		
		1. Why do we need eksctl?
		Without eksctl, you may need to configure multiple AWS resources manually, including the EKS cluster, networking, IAM roles, and worker nodes.
		With eksctl, you can create a cluster using a single command.
		
		2. run: eksctl create cluster
        This creates an EKS cluster using default settings, subject to your AWS permissions, quotas, and available resources.

